WEBVTT

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.930
How many times do I have to tell him?

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.320
I bet their parents never 
taught them manners!

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.440
Who just came in that door?

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.240
Tsukishima-san? Maeyama-san?

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.750
I've told you a thousand 
times not to slam doors!

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.320
And what's more, you stink!

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.370
Go take a bath!

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.060
You're distracting me!

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.750
I can't work like this!

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.190
Both of you, apologize!

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.400
Apologize to Tsurumi-san.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.570
I made him last night!

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.140
Now both of you, apologize.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.590
Edogai-kun, don't waste your time 
on stuff like that. Do your job.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.170
Apologize to Tsurumi-san!

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.030
Tsurumi-san!

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.000
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.950
<b>Edogai Taxidermist</b>

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.950
They're finally done.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.170
Perfect fake skins.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.840
I started with six!

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.830
Tsurumi-san will be so happy!

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:38.330
He'll pat me on the head and 
tell me I did a good job!

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.450
Was that you, Maeyama-san?

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.260
How many times do I have to...

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:48.610
M-Maeyama-san?

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.100
<i>Who is that?</i>

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.450
<i>They're coming!</i>

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.820
<i>Did they come to steal the skins?</i>

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.930
<b>Episode Fourteen
Fakes</b>

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:11.400
The smoke's splitting when it 
comes out of the smokestack!

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.360
That means somebody's going 
to die in the mines again!

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.410
Stop it!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.850
Crap... Forgot my wallet.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:24.650
Hey, wasn't that one of Lt. Tsurumi's troops?

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.350
Maybe... Not sure.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:32.020
He must've come here because he heard rumors 
about a house with tattooed skins...

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.230
Let's follow him.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.230
Should we go get Kiroranke and Asirpa-chan?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.650
They're questioning people over there.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.950
No, there's no time.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.070
Let's go.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.060
I need to escape.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.120
But the only exit is the front door.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.590
What do I do?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.040
You gave me a rat as a present?

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.680
<i>Tsukishima takes long baths. 
He won't be back for a while.</i>

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:15.520
<i>I've got time to make the taxidermist 
tell me what they're planning here.</i>

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.090
Sir!

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:32.600
A white bear just went thataway...

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.890
I see. It's a scorcher out today, yeah.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.970
What the hell is this?

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:53.970
Looks like the taxidermist kid 
is in love with Lt. Tsurumi.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.470
Well, that's not good.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:06.580
It gives Lt. Tsurumi too 
much of an advantage.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.580
Shit. He got away!

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:27.010
You bastard!

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.300
You'll pay for what you did to Maeyama...

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.640
How could you kill your
former comrade, Ogata?

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.270
Both of you are working 
against the government.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:39.440
You're HQ's pet cat!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.320
I know exactly what you want!

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:46.320
You want to offer rebels up to the 
government so you can get a promotion.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:49.490
You want to sell out your friends 
so you can surpass your father,

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.980
who was the head of the 7th Division!

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:54.200
Friends, comrades?

00:05:54.200 --> 00:06:00.380
You're good at using cheesy lines 
to trick young men, Lt. Tsurumi.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.670
<i>How many bullets do I have left?</i>

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.010
Edogai, you alive?

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:20.730
A white bear just went thataway...

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.520
Was that him?

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.530
I need to give them to Tsurumi-san!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.170
He went after Edogai?

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:43.460
I need to find him before Tsukishima...

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:46.900
Can we ignore the soldier who just ran out?

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.430
I want to know what's in this house.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.770
<i>Immortal Sugimoto...</i>

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:55.010
<i>Well, that's another problem to worry about.</i>

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.560
Look, Sugimoto! A body!

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.020
That's suspicious! This might be the place!

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.320
What the hell is this?

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.290
You're Shiraishi Yoshitake, aren't you?

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.410
Hijikata Toshizou told me about you.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:21.210
<i>Should I make them stop Tsukishima for me?</i>

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.540
Sugimoto!

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.810
Look at this!

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:30.790
I think Lt. Tsurumi was 
making fake skins here!

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:35.050
The soldier who just left 
must have stolen them!

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.140
We should chase him now!

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.260
Tsurumi-san! Tsurumi-san!

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.450
Did you see a white bear?

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.010
Tsurumi-san! Tsurumi-san! Tsurumi-san!

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.760
Edogai-kun!

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:19.350
Your luck ran out when you met the 
Grim Reaper named Lt. Tsurumi.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.340
Get on, Edogai!

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:29.730
That's him!

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.680
Tsukishima-san, let's head 
into the tunnels and escape!

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.660
The tunnels all loop back on each other,
and there are plenty of exits!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.980
I'm going to get the fake 
skins I made to Tsurumi-san

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.070
and have him pat me on the head and lick me!

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.550
Tsurumi-san!

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.090
Immortal Sugimoto?!

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.760
Did he hear the rumors 
about the tattooed skins?

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.160
We can't let them get away!

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:09.230
If those fake skins get loose,
 there'll be chaos!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.000
Ow!

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:26.830
Get lost!

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:30.820
Watch out!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.590
Oh, no... They'll catch up to us!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.930
Give me those skins!

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.060
Get lost!

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:49.980
Watch out, Shiraishi!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.940
My pants are gonna split!

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:13.420
It's the guy who killed Maeyama-san!

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:15.040
That's Ogata.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.050
Keep your head down or he'll shoot!

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.170
Hey!

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:19.480
Stop! Stop!

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:20.980
We lit the 'mite up!

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:23.850
Stop, or you'll be caught in the explosion!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:24.500
Oh, no!

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.410
Were they yelling something?

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.350
Not sure.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.540
Dynamite? That was close.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:37.990
That scared me.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.720
But now they can't follow us!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.380
Let's escape out the other 
side of the mountain!

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.170
Shit.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.630
Hey, do you smell something?

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:51.880
Like burning metal...

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:59.010
Firedamp!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.290
The blast hit a gas pocket!

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:02.090
Run!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.970
It's gonna blow!

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.990
Did something just blow up?

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.940
Let's just get out of here, Shiraishi!

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:26.660
What's this wind?

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.620
It's a returner!

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.830
There might be another, bigger blast!

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:35.460
Get out, now!

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:44.010
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.970
Another gas explosion...

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:52.040
That was the biggest we've 
had for a long while.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.770
The whole mountain shook.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.170
That's terrible!

00:11:58.390 --> 00:11:59.380
Edogai!

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:04.280
Where are you, Edogai? Are you still alive?

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:08.240
Tsukishima-san, I'm right here!

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:11.200
Over there?

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.070
I'll get you out now!

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:16.840
Tsukishima-san, run away.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:22.140
The only way to keep the fire from 
spreading is to shut off the air.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.620
So they'll seal all the exits,

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.790
even if there are still people inside.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:29.080
Then we need to get you out!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:33.780
A rock crushed my leg...

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.690
Take this to Tsurumi-san!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.200
He was the first person 
who ever took me seriously.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.700
And this was what he wanted in return.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:52.200
Don't waste them, Tsukishima-san!

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.080
Right!

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:56.120
And one more thing....

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.880
There's one more thing 
I want you to tell him.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.840
What is it? Tell me, Edogai!

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:08.180
Shiraishi! Wake up, Shiraishi!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.280
Wake up, you useless idiot!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:20.370
<i>I feel so tired... Is it because of the gas?</i>

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:29.030
I am Immortal Sugimoto!

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:50.530
I don't know where I'm going!
 That's not good.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:57.300
Hey, not that way!

00:13:57.300 --> 00:14:00.150
The air vent's this way! Come this way!

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:20.330
Why the hell...

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:38.400
Shiraishi, breathe!

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.480
I can't have you dying on me!

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.820
Shiraishi! Shiraishi!

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.460
<i>Shit... not here...</i>

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:01.540
Somebody's coming out!

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:03.720
Did someone just now make it out?

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:07.510
Wow! He saved two of them!

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:19.430
Hey, girl. We meet again.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.830
Dick-sensei!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:27.570
The fish cake! She's still got it!

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:37.600
What are you doing here?

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:41.620
I came with someone else 
to Yuubari, but they disappeared.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:45.560
I was looking for them when 
I saw you on that mine cart.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:46.440
Someone else?

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:53.550
Fine. Take them with us.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.840
You were with Lt. Tsurumi!

00:15:56.840 --> 00:15:58.520
Why are you with Ushiyama?

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:07.690
The fakes were probably made 
using these six bodies.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:11.270
We know for a fact that 
the taxidermist is dead.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:14.160
Sergeant Tsukishima is a tough soldier.

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:17.290
Until they pull his body out of the tunnels,

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:22.230
we have to assume there are six fake 
skins in circulation out there.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:40.430
We need to find a way to tell if the 
one he left behind is fake or real.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:54.180
Old man, have we met?

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.160
<i>Shit!</i>

00:16:57.770 --> 00:17:00.370
No, don't be silly!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.200
This is Hijikata Toshizou!

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:04.170
Hijikata...

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:08.520
It's been a long time, Shiraishi Yoshitake.

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:11.410
Will you introduce me to your friend?

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:15.130
<i>What's the plan if he finds out,
you senile old geezer?!</i>

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:19.640
<i>Will Sugimoto kill me if he finds out 
I've been passing them information?</i>

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:23.280
There was something I wanted 
to ask you if we met.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:27.720
There's something that Nopperabo 
must've told you and nobody else.

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:30.330
Either he trusted you to a degree,

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:33.560
or you both shared some great goal.
 I don't know which.

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:38.900
But did he propose that you give weapons to 
the Ainu and start a war of independence?

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:44.130
Is Nopperabo really an Ainu?

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:49.250
You've gotten that far, huh?

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:56.320
Is your plan to get one up on Nopperabo 
and rebuild the Republic of Ezo,

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.150
Hijikata Toshizou-san?

00:17:58.760 --> 00:17:59.800
My father is—

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.300
Do we work together,

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:03.690
or do we kill each other here?

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:05.770
Choose.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:11.590
<i>Hijikata just cut that girl's words off.</i>

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.430
<i>"My father"?</i>

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:17.720
<i>Is that girl Nopperabo's daughter?</i>

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:25.370
If you have tattooed skins, 
we'll buy them from you.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.500
<i>Nagakura Shinpachi is here, too!</i>

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.780
We won't ask you to help us.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:38.170
Just sell us the skins, and use the money 
to go home, find a wife, and live in peace.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:41.910
Or is that too boring a life for a young man?

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:46.190
I need to meet Nopperabo
 and find some answers.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:49.380
Until then, I can't have you finding the gold.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:01.160
What the hell is with that rumbling?

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:06.530
Shall I make something for you?

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.740
Ienaga's alive!

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:14.210
Why not discuss the rest over a meal?

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.620
This is nanko stew.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.400
It's a local dish made in the Sorachi area,
which includes Yuubari.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:41.000
An offal stew made from 
boiling intestines in miso.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:44.690
Hey, Ienaga. This meat's safe to eat, right?

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:46.080
Don't worry!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.770
Nanko means "horse intestine" 
in the local dialect.

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:51.080
Horse, eh?

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:55.040
I don't know how all you guys 
manage to work together.

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:58.900
Especially the guy who used 
to work for Lt. Tsurumi.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:03.010
Somebody who's a traitor 
once will betray you again.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:09.330
Sugimoto, you almost killed me,
 but I'm not the type to hold a grudge.

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:11.480
That hurt me, though.

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:16.940
No fighting during lunch.

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:22.950
Our priority right now is finding a way
 to tell which ones are the fakes.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:30.830
<b>Otaru</b>

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:33.040
I have returned.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:40.460
The highest ambition of an artist is to 
leave his work behind for the world to enjoy.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:44.760
Especially if it's something 
that will change the world,

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:46.200
they could ask for no more.

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:51.390
Edogai's last words were a message for you.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:52.850
What is it?

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.890
Iron! Tell him "Iron"!

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:57.860
"Iron"?

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:02.760
Tsurumi-san... He'll be able to 
figure it out just from that!

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:08.280
Well done.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:10.320
Get some rest, Tsukishima.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.240
Yes, sir.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:16.710
Iron... Iron...

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:21.210
<i>Edogai had an obsession with tannin.</i>

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:24.170
<i>It's a way of tanning that 
takes a lot of extra effort,</i>

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:26.930
<i>that no one else would ever use.</i>

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:30.120
<i>He shared that with me and no one else.</i>

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:38.100
Tsurumi-san, when these 
gloves get wet, be careful!

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:43.110
If they touch a certain thing,
 they'll turn black!

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:50.600
<i>The tannin gets absorbed into the 
water and then reacts with the iron.</i>

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:55.580
<i>Edogai-kun's last words were telling 
me how to detect the fakes.</i>

00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:00.500
<i>He sacrificed his life to 
give me five fake skins.</i>

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:03.560
<i>And I'll make good use of them!</i>

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time
Let's Talk About the Past</b>

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:40.250
Next Time: "Let's Talk About the Past."
